0eaffc7af0a36fcd11640ff3ea4e5bd38e\", \"fd0a340b26283ef9ef5ba20f2f5bae3c6b8a8bf77ddadb4547971a228ad226c1\", \"f8a232bd43d936a35570c6eace031f7fbebf1af0ef7348edb7113f63ec293748\", \"5612ad20b83228b0963ff7a170c3a0e8ed3b40d91e8059427e8e17e59908883e\", \"6aacc2fc9f91f52344143213e0bec8578807f5b88b140cd2026acd226fc7bcb9\", \"1e8d1f1241226a3f8d182f77c205ad5062c23664b03c7627d52878e7c55ad991\", \"f1094ba2d35fb263302c3c27b42881e2b714631df781d76b0975caf735456f9a\", \"8548d0f643200589f6a97bdd7a487c699fc5d83b3eda9cde6f1b438ba2b30231\", \"77ba1cdde466c22225ce19e15344c09ee5bed726561ad4136cfc3034fb0c7beb\", \"6e18ef68610b5c3b21c5fd1cb35fc0e2d33226e7743a728abdc6f7815212def4\", \"29679dbcc821686c0effff37f5e7580f4e356e3bef90522ae7c424178cc0a68b\", \"3a1f88732a57f229ebfe92b0acb7b8c601d9dd6cb8aa696576b113b95e7dc50f\", \"dc822c2395a244d34d6c263c9a2ee5b3d0b7a63d6418670b162f692cce100800\", \"6b6119b506cf750b9414a73a8261c8a81adac38cb78734d556128a9005a07706\", \"cb5fc0bbc2cc91e6f97fe14a81ba010299bf50a55b98d8b15f33cb811589d315\", \"7c7a4d3efda31be1b73f9d7262ab075021bb1b760b86672a7cf11753fa296eed\", \"e3a0f0b0c4035da789178819dc06284c75c0263f46b79c67617dd7abed93e0ce\", \"0c176cfdb7fe9453dd056a3434cd8366b5c35fe38a75cb9ace02a2a472e4334e\", \"ae5419e23cfae5549791fd181169ce95b85d17dadf6de4128d2db58600066ee7\"],\n  \"reviewerType\": \"llm-vision-headless-cli\",\n  \"summary\": \"The export/migration surfaces have genuinely good domain copy in places -- 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified', 'Snapshot E-204 is the last good state', '48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible' all read as real product content, and the community name is in the app bar on every non-modal screen. But two whole workflows are not actually demonstrated: all three export-redacted-bundle screenshots are byte-identical to the export-full-bundle ones and show the heading 'Full export bundle', and the export-import-replay action/complete screenshots are byte-identical to export-import-preview and show 'Legacy import preview' with no replay-specific state. Separately, every 'action' screenshot is the same static explainer sheet -- an 'Export steps' list plus an identical 'Export workspace / Export scope / Verification and recovery' boilerplate block -- with zero interactive controls and no evidence that any action was performed, so the in-progress state is not legible anywhere. Copy also leaks other communities' domains into this one ('Provider Cloud HOA', 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone', 'guardian or coach visibility policy'), and several cards clip their titles ('Provider transfer roll...', 'Exportable custom-sc...').\",\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. The workflow is usually named -- 'Full export bundle', 'Provider transfer verification', 'Provider rollback plan', 'Exportable schema catalog', 'Checksum evidence record' all appear as large page headings under a 'Data Portability Community' app bar -- and the complete screens do carry a distinct outcome banner ('Transfer verified', 'Rollback ready', 'Schema scope saved', 'Checksum verified', 'Export bundle generated'). But the state axis breaks down in two ways. First, the 'action' screenshots are indistinguishable from a static help sheet: each one is a full-screen modal titled with the workflow name containing the same numbered 'Export steps' list already visible on the start screen, followed by the identical 'Export workspace / Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' block on all eight workflows. Nothing in those frames says an action is running, succeeded, or changed anything -- no spinner, no progress, no result row, and no buttons at all in the visible viewport. Second, two workflows show the wrong workflow entirely: export-redacted-bundle start/action/complete are pixel-identical to export-full-bundle and read 'Full export bundle', and export-import-replay action/complete are pixel-identical to export-import-preview and read 'Legacy import preview'. A user on those frames would conclude they are in a different workflow than the one being demonstrated.\",\n      \"score\": 34,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"export-redacted-bundle_start renders the heading 'Full export bundle' with subtitle 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.' -- the word 'redacted bundle' appears nowhere on the screen\",\n        \"export-import-replay_action shows the modal title 'Legacy import preview', not a replay surface, and is byte-identical to export-import-preview_action\",\n        \"All eight 'action' frames repeat the identical block 'Export workspace / Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' with no control or progress indicator visible\",\n        \"export-transfer-rollback_complete does show real completion state: 'Rollback ready' check chip plus 'Download file', 'Verify checksum', and 'Rollback' buttons under an 'After export' card\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-action\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"copy-accuracy\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the displayed text read as real product copy about this community's actual export content, or as generic/placeholder or borrowed-from-elsewhere copy?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Mixed, and the failures are specific rather than vague. The strong copy is genuinely strong: 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified', 'Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake', 'Checkpoint I-118 lets the owner retry or roll back the import', '48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible', 'Snapshot E-204 is the last good state and can be restored'. Those are concrete, identifier-bearing, and clearly about a data-portability product. The problems are (a) domain leakage from other communities -- 'Provider Cloud HOA' names an HOA in a community with no HOA context, and the redaction workflow describes 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone, care, vault, payment, and private notes are masked' with 'guardian or coach visibility policy', which is youth-sports content, not data-portability content; (b) card summaries in the feed are pure boilerplate -- three different cards on export-protected-redaction_start and export-transfer-rollback_start all carry the same truncated string 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...'; and (c) the 'Export workspace' descriptor block repeats verbatim on all eight action screens, which reads as scaffolding rather than copy.\",\n      \"score\": 48,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"export-transfer-verification_action step 1 reads 'Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake' -- an HOA reference inside the Data Portability Community\",\n        \"export-protected-redaction_action step 1 reads 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone, care, vault, payment, and private notes are masked' and step 2 references 'guardian or coach visibility policy'\",\n        \"On export-protected-redaction_start, both the 'Exportable custom-sc...' card and the 'Full export bundle' card carry the identical summary 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...'\",\n        \"export-checksum-evidence_start step 1 reads 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified' -- concrete, credible product copy\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"actionability\",\n      \"question\": \"Are the available actions clear on each screen, and is it clear why disabled or waiting affordances are in that state?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Only partly. The start screens surface a single well-labelled primary verb inside a 'Package progress' card -- 'Skip duplicate', 'Hold transfer', 'Reveal field' -- each paired with a sentence that explains what it does, and that pairing works well. Below it, though, the feed shows a page-level 'Generate export' button and then per-card 'Generate export' buttons on every subsequent card, so on export-import-replay_start there are three visually identical 'Generate export' targets on one viewport with nothing distinguishing their scope. Waiting affordances are unexplained: export-transfer-verification_start shows a 'Waiting' chip on the 'Provider transfer roll...' card whose only explanation is 'Waiting for the export package to be prepared' -- acceptable -- but export-transfer-rollback_start shows a bare 'Waiting' chip floating between two cards, detached from any card body, with no adjacent text at all. The action screens contain no tappable controls in the visible viewport whatsoever. The best case is export-transfer-rollback_complete, which shows 'Download file', 'Verify checksum', and 'Rollback' as clearly enabled outlined buttons under a 'Rollback ready' status chip.\",\n      \"score\": 45,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"export-import-replay_start shows three separate 'Generate export' buttons (one full-width, two inside minimized cards) with no scope differentiation\",\n        \"export-transfer-rollback_start shows an orphaned 'Waiting' chip sitting on its own between the 'Package progress' card and the 'Provider transfer roll...' card with no explanatory label\",\n        \"export-transfer-rollback_complete shows 'Download file', 'Verify checksum', and 'Rollback' buttons plus a 'Rollback ready' confirmation chip\",\n        \"None of the eight 'action' modal frames contain a single button in the visible viewport\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-action\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"visual-quality\",\n      \"question\": \"Is the visual execution production-grade -- no repeated generic card shells, no clipping or crowding, no thin/empty regions where content is expected?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. Three distinct visual defects recur. Title clipping: card headings truncate mid-word as 'Protected field routin...', 'Exportable custom-sc...', and 'Provider transfer roll...' while a much shorter 'Minimized' chip sits beside them consuming roughly a third of the row width. Repeated shells: the minimized cards are structurally identical -- download glyph, truncated title, 'Minimized' chip, then a fixed 2x2 button grid of 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Data package' / 'Expand' / 'Generate export' -- so the feed reads as the same shell stamped repeatedly. Empty regions: export-transfer-verification_start and export-transfer-rollback_start both end with a collapsed 'Local package details' row and then roughly 400px of pure empty background above the tab bar. Bottom-nav clipping is inconsistent across the set: export-import-replay_start and export-protected-redaction_start clip the 'Messages' tab label at the right edge ('Messages' with the final glyph cut), the transfer-verification and rollback screens drop the 'Admin' tab entirely and show only three tabs, and export-protected-redaction_start additionally clips a row of 'Expand' / 'Generate export' buttons horizontally at the bottom edge. Finally, export-protected-redaction_start opens with a cut-off text fragment 'actor are preserved.' sliced by the app bar.\",\n      \"score\": 38,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"export-import-replay_start shows card titles truncated to 'Protected field routin...' and 'Exportable custom-sc...' next to a wide 'Minimized' chip\",\n        \"export-transfer-verification_start and export-transfer-rollback_start both leave roughly 400px of empty dark background below the collapsed 'Local package details' row\",\n        \"export-protected-redaction_start clips the top text 'actor are preserved.' under the app bar and clips an 'Expand' / 'Generate export' button row at the bottom edge\",\n        \"Bottom nav is inconsistent: four tabs with 'Messages' clipped on the full-bundle/schema/checksum screens, only three tabs (Home/Documents/Messages, no Admin) on the transfer-verification and rollback screens\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screenReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This frame is scrolled past its own page heading, so the only thing tying it to the replay workflow is the 'Package progress' body text 'Resolve duplicate rows, confirm checkpoint I-118, then replay the import with retry and rollback available.' That sentence is good, specific copy and the paired 'Skip duplicate' button is a sensible primary verb. Below it the screen degrades: a full-width 'Generate export' button is followed by two minimized cards whose titles are truncated mid-word to 'Protected field routin...' and 'Exportable custom-sc...', each carrying a 'Minimized' chip and an identical 2x2 grid of 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Data package' / 'Expand' / 'Generate export'. That puts three separate 'Generate export' targets in one viewport with nothing indicating which scope each applies to. The 'Protected field routin...' card summary 'Protected youth roster profile includes minor-da...' is youth-sports content appearing in a data-portability community. The bottom nav clips the 'Messages' label at the right edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A replay start screen anchored by its own visible 'Import replay' heading, with card titles that wrap or ellipsize gracefully rather than mid-word, a single scoped export action, and card summaries describing this community's own export records rather than youth-roster data.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'Package progress' card: 'Resolve duplicate rows, confirm checkpoint I-118, then replay the import with retry and rollback available.'\",\n        \"'Skip duplicate' button with an arrow glyph inside the Package progress card\",\n        \"Three 'Generate export' buttons visible simultaneously\",\n        \"Truncated titles 'Protected field routin...' and 'Exportable custom-sc...' each with a 'Minimized' chip\",\n        \"Bottom nav 'Messages' label clipped at the right screen edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is it clear this is the start of the import-replay workflow rather than some other export workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only the sentence 'then replay the import with retry and rollback available' names replay; no heading reading 'replay' is on screen\",\n          \"why\": \"The workflow identity rests entirely on one line of body copy inside a subordinate card, because the frame is scrolled past the page title. A user landing here cannot name the workflow from the dominant visual elements.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the available actions clear, and is it clear why each is offered?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Three identical 'Generate export' buttons plus 'Skip duplicate', 'Tap for expanded view', 'Data package', and 'Expand'\",\n          \"why\": \"'Skip duplicate' is well explained by adjacent copy, but the repeated 'Generate export' buttons have no scope labels, so tapping any of them has an unpredictable result.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"9d033ba746f442d016568b6dedf98c2a6bf67c147620e632103abbb61727e5f7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This file is byte-identical to the export-import-preview action screenshot, and its modal title reads 'Legacy import preview' -- not a replay surface. Nothing on the frame shows a replay being executed: it is a static 'Export steps' list (1 Rows preview, 2 Conflict choices, 3 Replay checkpoint, 4 Import state, 5 Undo option) followed by the boilerplate 'Export workspace' block with 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' There is not a single button, spinner, progress bar, or state chip in the visible viewport, and the community name is absent because the modal app bar shows only 'X' and the sheet title. As evidence of an import-replay action state this frame is doubly invalid: wrong workflow surface, and no action state depicted. The step copy itself is good ('Checkpoint I-118 lets the owner retry or roll back the import'), but it is descriptive documentation, not an in-progress UI.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A replay-in-progress surface titled for the replay workflow showing which rows are being replayed, live progress against checkpoint I-118, and a visible stop/rollback control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Legacy import preview' with an 'X' close control\",\n        \"Numbered 'Export steps' 1-5 ending at '5 Undo option -- Owner can stop replay or roll back to checkpoint I-118.'\",\n        \"'Export workspace' block repeating 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.'\",\n        \"No buttons, no progress indicator, no status chip anywhere in the viewport\",\n        \"Byte-identical to the export-import-preview action screenshot\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this screen show an action being taken in the import-replay workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Title 'Legacy import preview'; content is a static numbered list with no controls\",\n          \"why\": \"The frame depicts a preview explainer, not a replay execution, so the action state of this workflow is entirely undocumented.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the persona/workflow scoping correct for what is being demonstrated?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Identical pixels and identical 'Legacy import preview' title as the import-preview workflow's action frame\",\n          \"why\": \"Two distinct workflows resolving to the same surface means the replay workflow either has no distinct UI or was never navigated to.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"3a1f88732a57f229ebfe92b0acb7b8c601d9dd6cb8aa696576b113b95e7dc50f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Byte-identical to the export-import-preview complete screenshot and headed 'Legacy import preview' with the subtitle 'Preview rows, conflicts, replay checkpoint, and rollback marker.' The completion banner at the bottom reads 'Import replay ready -- Import preview shows row counts, duplicate decisions, checkpoint, retry and rollback', which describes readiness to replay rather than a replay that completed. So the terminal state of the replay workflow is not evidenced: nothing shows rows actually replayed, no post-replay counts, no timestamp, no success/failure per record. The banner text is also clipped by the tab bar mid-sentence after 'retry and rollback', and the 'Export steps' card above it repeats the exact same five steps already shown on the start and action frames, so the complete frame adds almost no new information over the start frame. The app bar does correctly show 'Data Portability Community'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A replay-complete surface showing the replay outcome: rows applied vs skipped, the resolved duplicate decisions, the checkpoint the replay ran from, a completion timestamp, and rollback still offered.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Legacy import preview' with subtitle 'Preview rows, conflicts, replay checkpoint, and rollback marker.'\",\n        \"Completion banner 'Import replay ready' with body clipped mid-sentence at 'retry and rollback'\",\n        \"'Export steps' card identical to the one on the start and action frames\",\n        \"App bar shows 'Data Portability Community' with bell, message, and members icons\",\n        \"Byte-identical to export-import-preview_complete\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this screen make it clear the replay is complete rather than merely available?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner text 'Import replay ready' -- 'ready', not 'complete' or 'replayed'\",\n          \"why\": \"'Ready' communicates a pre-action state, so a user cannot tell from this frame that anything was replayed.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is content clipped or crowded?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The banner body ends at 'checkpoint, retry and rollback' where the white tab bar cuts it off\",\n          \"why\": \"The one element carrying the completion message is the element being truncated, so the most important copy on the screen is unreadable.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"dc822c2395a244d34d6c263c9a2ee5b3d0b7a63d6418670b162f692cce100800\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The strongest start screen in the set. The heading 'Full export bundle' with subtitle 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.' sits directly under the 'Data Portability Community' app bar, and the numbered 'Export steps' card gives five well-differentiated, domain-real steps: 'Bundle contents -- Members, receipts, documents, messages, custom records, and export metadata', 'Redaction -- Protected fields are counted and masked before download', 'Download -- Owner sees file size, checksum, download progress, and next transfer step', 'Owner artifact', 'Audit trail -- Scope, decision, timestamp, checksum, and actor are preserved'. Two flaws hold it below production grade: the persistent 'In-focus product surface / Expand' debug-looking strip pinned above the heading is scaffolding chrome, not product UI, and the 'Package progress' card at the bottom is sliced in half by the tab bar showing only its title, so the actual start-state progress and its primary action are invisible. The bottom nav also clips the 'Messages' label at the right edge.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The same heading and steps card without the 'In-focus product surface / Expand' harness strip, with the 'Package progress' card and its primary action fully visible above the tab bar.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'In-focus product surface' strip with an 'Expand' affordance pinned above the page heading\",\n        \"Heading 'Full export bundle' and subtitle 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.'\",\n        \"Five numbered export steps with distinct icons (folder, eye-off, download, download, history)\",\n        \"'Package progress' card title visible but its body cut off by the bottom tab bar\",\n        \"Bottom nav 'Messages' label clipped at the right screen edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow and its start state legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Full export bundle' heading plus 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Workflow identity is unambiguous and the steps read as not-yet-started, so start-state legibility is genuinely good here.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is any non-product chrome visible that would not ship?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'In-focus product surface' strip with 'Expand' at the top of the content area\",\n          \"why\": \"That label describes the capture harness rather than the product, and it occupies prime real estate directly above the page title.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6aacc2fc9f91f52344143213e0bec8578807f5b88b140cd2026acd226fc7bcb9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"A modal titled 'Full export bundle' that re-renders the identical five-step list from the start frame ('Bundle contents', 'Redaction', 'Download', 'Owner artifact', 'Audit trail') and then the generic 'Export workspace' block reading 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' with sub-items 'Export scope' and 'Verification and recovery'. Nothing indicates an action occurred: no bundle being assembled, no percentage, no file size accruing, no 'Generating...' state, and no controls of any kind in the visible viewport. The community app bar is replaced by a bare 'X' plus title, so the community context is lost inside the modal. The screen also ends mid-item on a repeated 'Bundle contents' row at the bottom edge, which is the same label already shown as step 1 above -- the same content appearing twice on one screen reads as a duplicated shell rather than a designed hierarchy.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A bundle-generation in-progress state showing live packaging progress, running file count and size, redaction count applied so far, and a cancel control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal header: 'X' and title 'Full export bundle', no community name\",\n        \"Same five numbered export steps as the start frame\",\n        \"'Export workspace' block with 'Export scope' and 'Verification and recovery' sub-items\",\n        \"'Bundle contents' label repeated at the bottom, duplicating step 1 above\",\n        \"Zero buttons or progress indicators in the viewport\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this frame demonstrate the in-progress state of generating a full export bundle?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Static step list plus 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Every element is descriptive future/general tense; nothing reports current activity, so the action state is not demonstrated.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is content repeated within the screen?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Bundle contents' appears as step 1 and again as a row under 'Export workspace'\",\n          \"why\": \"The same labelled content rendered twice in one viewport is a hallmark of a generic repeated card shell rather than purposeful layout.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"1e8d1f1241226a3f8d182f77c205ad5062c23664b03c7627d52878e7c55ad991\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Correct workflow and a real completion signal: the banner 'Export bundle generated -- Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress, and...' appears below the steps card, and the app bar restores 'Data Portability Community'. But the banner is the only new content on the screen relative to the start frame -- the five-step card above it is byte-for-byte the same list -- and the banner's body is clipped by the tab bar mid-phrase after 'download progress, and'. Critically, for a 'bundle generated' state, none of the actual result values are visible: no filename, no concrete file size, no checksum string, no redaction count, and no 'Download' button. The checksum workflow proves the app can render values like '18.4 MB' and '9A7F-PORT', so their absence here is a gap rather than a limitation. The screen therefore asserts completion without evidencing it.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A generated-bundle result showing the actual artifact: filename, byte size, checksum, redaction count, generation timestamp, and an enabled Download/Transfer control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"App bar 'Data Portability Community'; heading 'Full export bundle'\",\n        \"Completion banner 'Export bundle generated' with folder icon\",\n        \"Banner body clipped by the tab bar after 'checksum, file size, download progress, and'\",\n        \"Five-step card identical to the start frame\",\n        \"No filename, size, checksum value, or download button visible\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the complete state show the actual result of the export?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner says 'Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress' but no such values appear\",\n          \"why\": \"The copy promises concrete artifact metadata that the screen never renders, so completion is claimed rather than shown.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion message fully readable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Text ends at 'download progress, and' where the white tab bar overlays it\",\n          \"why\": \"The sentence is truncated at the bottom edge, cutting off the completion description.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"f1094ba2d35fb263302c3c27b42881e2b714631df781d76b0975caf735456f9a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Scrolled past its own heading, so the workflow is identified only by the 'Package progress' body 'Compare destination provider receipt with source package hash before confirming transfer.' paired with a 'Hold transfer' button -- that pairing is clear and well written. Below it the layout falls apart: a full-width 'Generate export' button, then a card whose title truncates to 'Provider transfer roll...' (which reads as the rollback workflow, not verification) carrying a 'Waiting' chip and body 'Waiting for the export package to be prepared.', then a collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure row, then roughly 400px of completely empty dark background before the tab bar. That dead zone in the lower fifth of the screen is exactly where a verification-status panel should live. The bottom nav here shows only three tabs -- Home, Documents, Messages -- with no 'Admin' tab, inconsistent with the full-bundle and schema screens which show four.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verification start state naming the workflow on screen, showing the source hash and the awaited provider receipt side by side, with the empty lower region filled by the verification status panel.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'Package progress': 'Compare destination provider receipt with source package hash before confirming transfer.' with a 'Hold transfer' button\",\n        \"Card title truncated to 'Provider transfer roll...' with a 'Minimized' chip and a 'Waiting' chip\",\n        \"Card body 'Waiting for the export package to be prepared.'\",\n        \"Collapsed 'Local package details' row with a chevron, followed by ~400px of empty background\",\n        \"Bottom nav shows only Home / Documents / Messages -- no Admin tab\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the lower portion of the screen carrying real content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Below 'Local package details' the frame is uniform dark background down to the tab bar\",\n          \"why\": \"A large empty region where verification status belongs is thin content, and it makes the screen read as unfinished.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the visible card match the verification workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The card title reads 'Provider transfer roll...' -- i.e. rollback -- on the verification screen\",\n          \"why\": \"Surfacing a rollback-titled card as the main content of the verification start state misdirects the user about which workflow they are in.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"7a81152c6ced9043dab56f38c37e0d3e646cf721b39b3889552a5c87ec4a7987\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Provider transfer verification' with the best step copy in the set: '1 Destination -- Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake', '2 Hash match -- Source hash and provider receipt hash match before closeout', '3 Receipt -- Transfer receipt shows provider ID, timestamp, and status'. The identifiers E-204 and the named destination make this feel like real product content. Two problems. First, 'Provider Cloud HOA' names a homeowners association as the destination provider inside a Data Portability community with no HOA context anywhere else on these screens -- that is copy borrowed from another community's fixture. Second, as an action frame it shows no action: no hash comparison in flight, no receipt arriving, no verify button, and the screen ends mid-item on a repeated 'Destination' row under the generic 'Export workspace' block that duplicates step 1 verbatim. The modal also drops the community app bar entirely.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verification-in-flight state showing the source hash and provider receipt hash rendered side by side with a match/mismatch indicator and the receipt's provider ID and timestamp.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Provider transfer verification' with 'X' close\",\n        \"Step 1: 'Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake'\",\n        \"Step 2: 'Source hash and provider receipt hash match before closeout'\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate block identical to the other seven action frames\",\n        \"'Destination' row repeated at the bottom edge, duplicating step 1\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe this community's actual content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake'\",\n          \"why\": \"An HOA-named destination provider in a data-portability community indicates fixture copy carried over from a different community, undermining copy accuracy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is an action state visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only the static numbered steps and the 'Export workspace' descriptor block; no hash values, no controls\",\n          \"why\": \"Nothing on the frame distinguishes it from the workflow's explainer, so the verification action is undocumented.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"9f576b1e97ccbb7d431bcacb616aa28db06c7176530fe3ed5fdb8231c564d90c\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"One of the better complete frames. The app bar shows 'Data Portability Community', the heading 'Provider transfer verification' with subtitle 'Verify destination provider, handshake, receipt, and audit trail.' is fully visible, and the outcome banner reads 'Transfer verified -- Transfer verification shows provider, hash match, receipt, timestamp, and closeout state.' with a distinct destination icon, so the completed state is genuinely legible. It still falls short: the five-step card above the banner is verbatim the same list as the action frame, so the completion frame is ~85% repeated content; the actual verification result values are never shown (no source hash, no receipt hash, no provider ID, no timestamp -- only the assertion that they exist); the 'Provider Cloud HOA' copy leak persists in step 1; and the banner is cut off by the tab bar immediately below the second line. There is also no follow-on action offered after verification succeeds.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verified-transfer receipt showing the concrete matched hash pair, provider ID, closeout timestamp, and a next action such as 'View receipt' or 'Close out transfer'.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Provider transfer verification' with subtitle 'Verify destination provider, handshake, receipt, and audit trail.'\",\n        \"Outcome banner 'Transfer verified' with body 'shows provider, hash match, receipt, timestamp, and closeout state.'\",\n        \"Step 1 still reads 'Provider Cloud HOA receives bundle E-204 after handshake'\",\n        \"Steps card identical to the action frame's list\",\n        \"No hash values, provider ID, or timestamp actually rendered; no post-verification action button\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state distinguishable from the start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The 'Transfer verified' banner replaces the 'Package progress' card seen on the start frame\",\n          \"why\": \"The banner is a real, readable state change, which is why this screen scores better than the action frames on legibility.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the completion show verification evidence or just claim it?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner text lists 'provider, hash match, receipt, timestamp' but none of those values appear on screen\",\n          \"why\": \"For a verification workflow the evidence values are the product; describing them instead of rendering them leaves the completion unsubstantiated.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"a1c16428e75ffa4776bca2aa71329c0eaffc7af0a36fcd11640ff3ea4e5bd38e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The worst-composed frame in the set. It opens on a severed text fragment -- 'actor are preserved.' sliced horizontally by the app bar -- then a 'Package progress' card with genuinely good copy ('Apply the protected-field mask and keep before/after preview, policy reason, and reveal permission visible.') and a 'Reveal field' button. Below that the feed degenerates into stacked identical shells: an 'Exportable custom-sc...' card and a 'Full export bundle' card, both truncated or minimized, both carrying the exact same summary string 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...', both with the same 'Minimized' chip and the same 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Data package' button pair. The second card's action row is then clipped horizontally at the bottom, leaving half-rendered 'Expand' and 'Generate export' labels bleeding under the tab bar. The bottom nav additionally clips 'Messages'. Nothing on the frame names the redaction workflow at heading level.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A redaction start state anchored by its own visible heading, listing the specific protected fields queued for masking with their counts, without duplicate card shells sharing one boilerplate summary.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Top of content area shows the fragment 'actor are preserved.' cut by the app bar\",\n        \"'Package progress': 'Apply the protected-field mask and keep before/after preview, policy reason, and reveal permission visible.' with a 'Reveal field' button\",\n        \"'Exportable custom-sc...' and 'Full export bundle' cards both summarised 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...'\",\n        \"Bottom card's 'Expand' and 'Generate export' buttons clipped mid-glyph by the tab bar\",\n        \"Bottom nav 'Messages' label clipped at the right edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the cards visually distinguishable from one another?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Two cards with the identical summary 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...' and identical button grids\",\n          \"why\": \"Identical shells with identical copy are the definition of a repeated generic card, and the user has no basis for choosing between them.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is anything clipped or crowded?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'actor are preserved.' sliced at the top; 'Expand' / 'Generate export' sliced at the bottom\",\n          \"why\": \"Content is truncated at both edges of the viewport simultaneously, which reads as a broken scroll position rather than a designed screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"fd0a340b26283ef9ef5ba20f2f5bae3c6b8a8bf77ddadb4547971a228ad226c1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Protected redaction preview'. The step structure is coherent -- '1 Protected values', '2 Policy reason', '3 Before/after -- Owner compares source label, exported safe value, and redaction count', '4 Owner artifact', '5 Audit trail' -- but the substance is imported from a different community: step 1 reads 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone, care, vault, payment, and private notes are masked' and step 2 reads 'Each masked field shows guardian or coach visibility policy and the persona allowed to reveal it.' Guardians, coaches, minors, and rosters are youth-sports concepts; this community is a data-portability community with no such membership model, and the prompt's own framing says there is no persona system in this legacy schema, yet the copy references 'the persona allowed to reveal it'. As an action frame it again shows nothing happening: no before/after value pair, no redaction count, no mask being applied, no reveal control -- only the static list and the shared 'Export workspace' boilerplate block.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A live redaction preview showing an actual before/after value pair for at least one masked field with its policy reason and a running redaction count, described in this community's own domain terms.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Protected redaction preview' with 'X' close\",\n        \"Step 1: 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone, care, vault, payment, and private notes are masked.'\",\n        \"Step 2: 'Each masked field shows guardian or coach visibility policy and the persona allowed to reveal it.'\",\n        \"Step 3 promises a before/after comparison that the screen never renders\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate identical to the other action frames\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy describe this community's real content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone' and 'guardian or coach visibility policy'\",\n          \"why\": \"These are youth-sports domain terms with no referent in a data-portability community, so the copy is borrowed fixture text rather than accurate product copy.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the promised before/after comparison actually shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Step 3 says 'Owner compares source label, exported safe value, and redaction count' but no values are displayed\",\n          \"why\": \"The core artifact of a redaction preview is the masked-vs-unmasked pair, and it is described rather than rendered.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"f8a232bd43d936a35570c6eace031f7fbebf1af0ef7348edb7113f63ec293748\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Correct workflow and correctly headed: 'Protected redaction preview' with subtitle 'Mask protected fields with policy reasons before export.' under the 'Data Portability Community' app bar, and a completion banner reading 'Redaction applied' at the bottom. That banner is the sole differentiator from the action frame -- the five steps above it are identical -- and it is the most severely clipped banner in the set: only the title 'Redaction applied' and a single sliver of the following line survive above the tab bar, with the body text cut mid-height so glyphs are half-rendered. The result values a redaction-complete state needs are absent: no count of fields masked, no list of which fields, no before/after sample. The youth-roster copy leak ('Protected youth profile, minor roster phone... guardian or coach visibility policy') persists verbatim on this frame too.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A redaction-complete state showing how many fields were masked, which field classes they belonged to, the policy reason applied, and a sample masked value -- with the confirmation banner fully visible above the tab bar.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Protected redaction preview' and subtitle 'Mask protected fields with policy reasons before export.'\",\n        \"Completion banner 'Redaction applied' with eye-off icon, body text sliced mid-glyph by the tab bar\",\n        \"Steps card identical to the action frame including the youth-roster copy\",\n        \"No masked-field count or before/after value visible\",\n        \"Bottom nav shows four tabs: Home, Documents, Admin, Messages\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion confirmation fully readable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only 'Redaction applied' plus a half-height sliver of the next line is visible before the tab bar\",\n          \"why\": \"The confirmation body is cut through the middle of its glyphs, which is visible clipping of the screen's most important element.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the complete state add information over the action state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The five-step card is byte-equivalent to the action frame; only the banner differs\",\n          \"why\": \"A completion screen that repeats the explainer and adds one clipped line gives the user almost no new information about what was redacted.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"5612ad20b83228b0963ff7a170c3a0e8ed3b40d91e8059427e8e17e59908883e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This screenshot is byte-identical (sha256 6aacc2fc...) to the export-full-bundle start screenshot and renders the heading 'Full export bundle' with the subtitle 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.' The words 'redacted bundle' appear nowhere on the screen. The five steps shown -- 'Bundle contents', 'Redaction', 'Download', 'Owner artifact', 'Audit trail' -- are the full-bundle steps; the 'Redaction' step here is a single line inside the full-bundle flow ('Protected fields are counted and masked before download'), not a redacted-bundle workflow surface. As evidence for the export-redacted-bundle workflow this frame is invalid: a user looking at it would correctly conclude they are in the full-bundle workflow. The same harness strip 'In-focus product surface / Expand' and the same clipped 'Package progress' card and clipped 'Messages' nav label carry over.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A redacted-bundle start screen headed for that workflow, showing which fields will be stripped from the bundle and how the redacted package differs from the full one.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading reads 'Full export bundle', not redacted bundle\",\n        \"Identical sha256 to B16_ext_export_migration_export-full-bundle_start.png\",\n        \"'In-focus product surface' harness strip above the heading\",\n        \"'Package progress' card title visible with body cut off by the tab bar\",\n        \"Bottom nav 'Messages' label clipped at the right edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does this screen show the redacted-bundle workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Large heading 'Full export bundle' with subtitle 'Generate a downloadable package with scope, redaction, and checksum.'\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen names a different workflow, so the redacted-bundle start state has no evidence at all in this catalog.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Can a user tell which workflow they are in?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Nothing on the frame contains the word 'redacted' as a heading or state label\",\n          \"why\": \"Context legibility fails outright when the screen self-identifies as a different workflow than the one under review.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6aacc2fc9f91f52344143213e0bec8578807f5b88b140cd2026acd226fc7bcb9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Byte-identical (sha256 1e8d1f12...) to the export-full-bundle action screenshot. The modal is titled 'Full export bundle' and contains the full-bundle step list plus the generic 'Export workspace' block. There is no redaction-specific content, no indication of fields being stripped, no redacted vs full comparison, and -- as with every action frame in this set -- no controls, no progress, and no evidence that any action was taken. The modal drops the 'Data Portability Community' app bar in favour of a bare 'X' and title, so even the community context is unavailable. This frame fails on two independent axes simultaneously: wrong workflow, and no action state.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A redacted-bundle generation in progress showing fields being stripped, a running count of redactions applied, and the resulting reduced scope compared against the full bundle.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Full export bundle', not a redacted-bundle title\",\n        \"Identical sha256 to B16_ext_export_migration_export-full-bundle_action.png\",\n        \"Full-bundle step list: 'Bundle contents', 'Redaction', 'Download', 'Owner artifact', 'Audit trail'\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate block identical to all other action frames\",\n        \"No buttons, progress indicator, or state chip visible\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow scoping correct?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Modal titled 'Full export bundle' on the redacted-bundle action row\",\n          \"why\": \"The evidence row claims to demonstrate the redacted-bundle action but the pixels show a different workflow's modal.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is an action state visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Static numbered steps and the 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' descriptor\",\n          \"why\": \"No element on the frame reports current activity, so nothing distinguishes this from a help sheet.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"1e8d1f1241226a3f8d182f77c205ad5062c23664b03c7627d52878e7c55ad991\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Byte-identical (sha256 f1094ba2...) to the export-full-bundle complete screenshot. The heading reads 'Full export bundle' and the completion banner reads 'Export bundle generated -- Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress, and...' -- the banner explicitly names the full bundle, so it actively contradicts the redacted-bundle workflow it is filed under. Beyond the misattribution, the same completion gaps apply: no redacted artifact filename, no redaction count, no file size, no checksum, no download control, and the banner body is clipped by the tab bar mid-sentence. There is no way for a user or reviewer to confirm from this frame that a redacted bundle was ever produced.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A redacted-bundle-complete state naming the redacted artifact, its size and checksum, the number of fields redacted, and an enabled download action for the redacted package specifically.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Full export bundle'; banner 'Export bundle generated'\",\n        \"Banner body explicitly reads 'Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress, and'\",\n        \"Identical sha256 to B16_ext_export_migration_export-full-bundle_complete.png\",\n        \"Banner body clipped by the tab bar mid-sentence\",\n        \"No redaction count, artifact name, size, checksum, or download button\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the completion banner refer to the redacted bundle?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner body: 'Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size...'\",\n          \"why\": \"The banner names the full bundle by name, so the frame documents the wrong workflow's completion.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there any redaction-specific outcome data?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"No count, field list, or masked sample appears anywhere on the frame\",\n          \"why\": \"Without redaction-specific results the screen cannot serve as evidence that a redacted bundle differs from a full one.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"f1094ba2d35fb263302c3c27b42881e2b714631df781d76b0975caf735456f9a\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Scrolled past its own heading and, worse, the visible 'Package progress' copy belongs to the verification workflow, not rollback: 'Compare destination provider receipt with source package hash before confirming transfer.' with a 'Hold transfer' button. Nothing on the frame mentions mismatch, snapshot, or rollback except the truncated card title 'Provider transfer roll...'. That card's summary is the same generic string seen on the redaction screen -- 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...' -- which contradicts the verification screen where the same card read 'Waiting for the export package to be prepared'. A bare 'Waiting' chip floats between the 'Package progress' card and the card below it, attached to no visible container and with no accompanying label, which reads as a layout bug. The lower ~400px below the collapsed 'Local package details' row is entirely empty. Bottom nav shows three tabs, missing 'Admin'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A rollback start state naming the workflow, stating the detected mismatch and the snapshot (E-204) available for restore, with a clearly labelled restore action and no orphaned status chips.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'Package progress' copy is about transfer verification: 'Compare destination provider receipt with source package hash before confirming transfer.'\",\n        \"'Hold transfer' button, not a rollback action\",\n        \"Orphaned 'Waiting' chip floating between two cards with no container or label\",\n        \"Card title truncated to 'Provider transfer roll...' with summary 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...'\",\n        \"~400px of empty background below 'Local package details'; bottom nav missing the Admin tab\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the visible copy describe the rollback workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Compare destination provider receipt with source package hash before confirming transfer.' with a 'Hold transfer' button\",\n          \"why\": \"That is verification copy; the rollback start state is therefore not identifiable from this frame.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are there layout defects?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"A 'Waiting' chip sits alone at the right, vertically between two cards, unattached to either\",\n          \"why\": \"A status chip rendered outside any card boundary is an obvious layout escape rather than intentional composition.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"8548d0f643200589f6a97bdd7a487c699fc5d83b3eda9cde6f1b438ba2b30231\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Provider rollback plan' with the most substantive step copy in the whole set: '1 Mismatch -- Destination provider hash differs from source package checksum', '2 Rollback checkpoint -- Snapshot E-204 is the last good state and can be restored', '3 Recovery audit -- Audit logs who started rollback, time, scope, and restored status', '4 Restored state', '5 Retry option -- Owner can retry transfer after provider mismatch is resolved'. The mismatch reason and the named snapshot make the workflow unambiguous, and the icons (alert, undo, history, history, refresh) are meaningfully differentiated. The failure is the same structural one as every other action frame: no rollback is actually in progress. There is no restore control, no progress, no 'rolling back...' state, and the frame ends on a duplicated 'Mismatch' row beneath the shared 'Export workspace' boilerplate, repeating step 1 within the same viewport. The community app bar is replaced by a bare 'X'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A rollback-in-progress state showing restore progress against snapshot E-204, which record types have been reverted so far, and a visible abort control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Provider rollback plan'\",\n        \"Step 1 'Mismatch -- Destination provider hash differs from source package checksum.'\",\n        \"Step 2 'Snapshot E-204 is the last good state and can be restored.'\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate block, then a repeated 'Mismatch' row at the bottom edge\",\n        \"No restore/abort controls or progress indicator anywhere\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the workflow and its cause legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Destination provider hash differs from source package checksum' and 'Snapshot E-204 is the last good state'\",\n          \"why\": \"This is the clearest workflow framing in the set -- the user learns both why rollback is needed and what will be restored.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the frame show the action being performed?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Static plan steps only; the word 'plan' in the title itself signals a pre-action state\",\n          \"why\": \"A plan is not an execution, so the rollback action state remains undocumented.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"77ba1cdde466c22225ce19e15344c09ee5bed726561ad4136cfc3034fb0c7beb\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The best screen in the set and the only one that reads as a genuine post-action state. Under the 'Data Portability Community' app bar it shows a summary line 'Rollback plan shows mismatch reason, checkpoint, restore action, retry option, and recovery audit.', then an 'After export' card explaining 'The saved result keeps status, history, and change actions visible for this community task.' with two concrete outcome rows -- 'Restored state -- Records return to snapshot E-204 and destination status is marked rolled back.' and 'Retry option -- Owner can retry transfer after provider mismatch is resolved.' -- followed by three enabled outlined buttons 'Download file', 'Verify checksum', 'Rollback' and a checkmark chip 'Rollback ready'. Remaining defects: the status chip says 'Rollback ready' on a screen documenting a completed rollback, which contradicts 'is marked rolled back' two lines above; a 'Rollback' button is still offered after rollback, with no explanation of whether it repeats or is a no-op; the 'After export' card body text renders at noticeably lower contrast (dark grey on dark grey) than surrounding text, hurting legibility; and roughly 300px below 'Local package details' is empty. Bottom nav again shows only three tabs.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The same result card with a status chip that reads as completed (e.g. 'Rolled back') consistent with the body copy, adequate text contrast, and the post-rollback actions labelled so their effect after completion is unambiguous.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'After export' card: 'The saved result keeps status, history, and change actions visible for this community task.'\",\n        \"'Restored state -- Records return to snapshot E-204 and destination status is marked rolled back.'\",\n        \"Buttons 'Download file', 'Verify checksum', 'Rollback' all rendered as enabled outlined controls\",\n        \"Checkmark chip reading 'Rollback ready'\",\n        \"'After export' body text renders at low contrast against the card background; ~300px empty region below 'Local package details'\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state legible and consistent?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Body says 'destination status is marked rolled back' while the chip says 'Rollback ready'\",\n          \"why\": \"The outcome is clearly communicated by the body copy, but the status chip states a pre-action readiness that contradicts it.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the offered actions clear after completion?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"A 'Rollback' button remains enabled alongside 'Download file' and 'Verify checksum'\",\n          \"why\": \"Offering the just-completed destructive action again with no disabled state or explanatory label leaves its effect ambiguous.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6e18ef68610b5c3b21c5fd1cb35fc0e2d33226e7743a728abdc6f7815212def4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"A solid start frame. The 'Data Portability Community' app bar sits above the heading 'Legacy import preview' with subtitle 'Preview rows, conflicts, replay checkpoint, and rollback marker.', and the five 'Export steps' carry the most concrete numbers in the set: '48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible', 'Duplicates can be accepted, skipped, or held for owner decision', 'Checkpoint I-118 lets the owner retry or roll back the import'. That reads as real product content about a real import. The defects are at the edges: the 'Package progress' card at the bottom is cut mid-sentence by the tab bar at 'then replay the import with retry and rollback', so the start state's primary action is not visible on this frame; and the bottom nav clips the 'Messages' label. The 'three duplicate records' phrasing is also inconsistent with the numeric style of '48', '22', '12' in the same sentence.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The same heading and steps with the 'Package progress' card and its primary action fully visible above the tab bar, and consistent numeral formatting within a single sentence.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"App bar 'Data Portability Community'; heading 'Legacy import preview'\",\n        \"Step 1: '48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible.'\",\n        \"Step 3: 'Checkpoint I-118 lets the owner retry or roll back the import.'\",\n        \"'Package progress' card clipped mid-sentence at 'then replay the import with retry and rollback'\",\n        \"Bottom nav 'Messages' label clipped at the right edge\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy read as real content about this community's import?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible.'\",\n          \"why\": \"Specific counts plus a named checkpoint identifier make this credible product copy rather than placeholder text.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the start-state action visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The 'Package progress' card is sliced by the tab bar before any button renders\",\n          \"why\": \"The frame shows the workflow clearly but omits the affordance that would let a user begin it.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"29679dbcc821686c0effff37f5e7580f4e356e3bef90522ae7c424178cc0a68b\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Legacy import preview' repeating the same five steps already fully visible on the preview start frame, followed by the shared 'Export workspace' block and a duplicated 'Rows preview' row at the bottom edge that restates step 1. For a preview workflow, this is where the actual previewed rows should appear -- the copy promises '48 members, 22 documents, 12 receipts, and three duplicate records are visible' but no row list, no table, and no duplicate records are rendered anywhere. There are no conflict-resolution controls despite step 2 stating 'Duplicates can be accepted, skipped, or held for owner decision'; not one of those three choices appears as a control. The modal also drops the community app bar. This same file is additionally filed as the import-replay action evidence, so one surface is standing in for two workflows.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An actual preview surface listing the importable rows with the three duplicate records flagged, plus Accept / Skip / Hold controls attached to each conflict.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Legacy import preview' with 'X' close, no community name\",\n        \"Steps 1-5 identical to the start frame\",\n        \"Step 2 names three conflict choices but no Accept/Skip/Hold controls appear\",\n        \"'Rows preview' label repeated at the bottom, duplicating step 1\",\n        \"Byte-identical to export-import-replay_action\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the preview screen actually preview anything?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Step 1 claims rows 'are visible' but no rows, table, or duplicate records are rendered\",\n          \"why\": \"The screen describes a preview instead of presenting one, so the workflow's central content is missing.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the stated conflict actions actionable?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Duplicates can be accepted, skipped, or held for owner decision' appears as body text with no adjacent controls\",\n          \"why\": \"Naming three decisions without offering them as controls makes the described actionability unverifiable on this screen.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"3a1f88732a57f229ebfe92b0acb7b8c601d9dd6cb8aa696576b113b95e7dc50f\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Headed 'Legacy import preview' under the community app bar, with the completion banner 'Import replay ready -- Import preview shows row counts, duplicate decisions, checkpoint, retry and rollback' clipped mid-sentence at the tab bar. Two problems specific to this row. First, the banner announces replay readiness, which is the neighbouring workflow's outcome, not 'preview complete' -- a preview-complete state should confirm the preview was reviewed and the conflict decisions recorded. Second, the promised 'duplicate decisions' are nowhere on screen: no record of which of the three duplicates were accepted, skipped, or held. The five-step card above is verbatim identical to the start and action frames, so the frame contributes one clipped line of new information. This same file also serves as the import-replay complete evidence.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A preview-complete state showing the recorded decision for each of the three duplicate records, the confirmed row counts, and the checkpoint the import will run from.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"App bar 'Data Portability Community'; heading 'Legacy import preview'\",\n        \"Banner 'Import replay ready' with body clipped after 'checkpoint, retry and rollback'\",\n        \"No duplicate decisions or per-row outcomes displayed\",\n        \"Steps card identical to the start and action frames\",\n        \"Byte-identical to export-import-replay_complete\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the completion state match this workflow?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner reads 'Import replay ready', not a preview-complete confirmation\",\n          \"why\": \"The terminal message describes the next workflow's readiness rather than this workflow's outcome, blurring which workflow completed.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Are the duplicate decisions the preview promised visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner claims 'shows row counts, duplicate decisions' but no decisions are rendered\",\n          \"why\": \"The outcome data that would prove the preview was completed is described rather than shown.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"dc822c2395a244d34d6c263c9a2ee5b3d0b7a63d6418670b162f692cce100800\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Clear and well-scoped. Heading 'Exportable schema catalog' with subtitle 'List schemas, field classes, custom records, and history.' under the community app bar, and the steps enumerate genuine schema-domain content: 'Schema list -- community, member, receipt, document, message, task, event, and custom tables', 'Field classes -- Public, member, protected, payment, audit, and custom field classes are shown', 'Version history -- Each schema row includes version, owner, and last export progress'. The lowercase table names in step 1 sit oddly against the sentence-case elsewhere but read as deliberate identifier styling. Two failures: the 'In-focus product surface / Expand' harness strip again sits above the page title, and -- more materially for a catalog workflow -- no actual schema rows are listed anywhere on the frame. The screen describes a catalog rather than showing one, and the 'Package progress' card that would carry the start action is sliced to a bare title by the tab bar.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"An actual catalog listing the eight named tables as rows with their field-class badges, version numbers, and include/exclude toggles -- without the capture-harness strip.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'In-focus product surface' strip with 'Expand' above the heading\",\n        \"Heading 'Exportable schema catalog', subtitle 'List schemas, field classes, custom records, and history.'\",\n        \"Step 1 names eight tables: community, member, receipt, document, message, task, event, custom\",\n        \"Step 2 names six field classes: Public, member, protected, payment, audit, custom\",\n        \"'Package progress' card reduced to its title by the tab bar; no schema rows rendered\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does a catalog screen show a catalog?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Step 1 lists table names inside a sentence; no per-schema rows, badges, or toggles appear\",\n          \"why\": \"The eight tables are named in prose rather than presented as selectable catalog entries, so the workflow's core surface is absent.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is non-product chrome present?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'In-focus product surface' with 'Expand' pinned at the top of the content area\",\n          \"why\": \"This is capture-harness labelling occupying the position where product context should sit.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"6b6119b506cf750b9414a73a8261c8a81adac38cb78734d556128a9005a07706\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Exportable schema catalog' reproducing the same five steps from the start frame, then the shared 'Export workspace' block, then a duplicated 'Schema list' row at the bottom edge restating step 1. For the action state of a schema-selection workflow, the expected content is the include/exclude scope being set -- which tables the owner selected, which they excluded, the resulting record count. None of that is present: no checkboxes, no toggles, no counts, no selection summary, and no buttons at all in the viewport. The community app bar is replaced by a bare 'X' plus title. The step copy remains good ('Each schema row includes version, owner, and last export progress'), but it describes rows the screen never renders.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A schema-selection surface with the eight tables listed as toggleable rows showing version, owner, field classes, and a live count of records included in the export scope.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Exportable schema catalog' with 'X' close\",\n        \"Steps 1-5 identical to the start frame\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate identical to the other seven action frames\",\n        \"'Schema list' row repeated at the bottom, duplicating step 1\",\n        \"No toggles, checkboxes, counts, or buttons visible\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the action frame show schema scope being selected?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Only the static step list; no selection controls or scope counts appear\",\n          \"why\": \"Selecting export scope is the action this workflow exists to perform, and no part of it is depicted.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the content differentiated from the start frame?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The five steps are word-for-word the same as those on export-schema-listing_start\",\n          \"why\": \"Repeating the start frame's content inside a modal gives the user no signal that the state advanced.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"cb5fc0bbc2cc91e6f97fe14a81ba010299bf50a55b98d8b15f33cb811589d315\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Correct workflow, correct heading ('Exportable schema catalog' / 'List schemas, field classes, custom records, and history.'), community app bar present, and a real terminal banner: 'Schema scope saved -- Schema catalog shows exportable tables, field classes, history, and include/exclude scope.' with a schema icon. The word 'saved' genuinely signals completion, which is better than the 'ready' phrasing used on the import rows. It still fails on substance: the banner says an include/exclude scope is shown, but no scope is shown -- no list of included tables, no excluded ones, no record count, no saved timestamp. The steps card above is verbatim the start frame's, so the banner is the only delta, and the banner's second line is the last thing visible before the tab bar. Bottom nav shows four tabs here versus three on the transfer screens.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A saved-scope confirmation listing exactly which tables were included and excluded, the total record count in scope, and when the scope was saved.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Exportable schema catalog' under the 'Data Portability Community' app bar\",\n        \"Banner 'Schema scope saved' with body 'Schema catalog shows exportable tables, field classes, history, and include/exclude scope.'\",\n        \"No included/excluded table list or record count rendered\",\n        \"Steps card identical to the start frame\",\n        \"Bottom nav shows four tabs: Home, Documents, Admin, Messages\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completion clearly signalled?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Banner title 'Schema scope saved'\",\n          \"why\": \"'Saved' is unambiguous past-tense completion language, and the banner's distinct background separates it from the steps card.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the saved scope actually visible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The banner claims 'include/exclude scope' is shown but no table appears with an included or excluded state\",\n          \"why\": \"The saved artifact is asserted rather than displayed, so a user cannot confirm what they saved.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"7c7a4d3efda31be1b73f9d7262ab075021bb1b760b86672a7cf11753fa296eed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"The best copy in the catalog. Heading 'Checksum evidence record' with subtitle 'Verify digest, file count, byte size, and integrity receipt.' under the community app bar, and step 1 renders actual values -- 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified' -- which is exactly the concreteness missing from the other workflows' completion screens. Steps 2 and 3 are equally specific ('Source package hash and destination package hash must match', 'Receipt links checksum, scope, timestamp, and verifier identity'). Deductions: the 'In-focus product surface / Expand' harness strip sits above the heading again; the 'Package progress' card is reduced to its bare title by the tab bar so the start action is invisible; and step 1 already declares 'SHA-256 verified' on the *start* frame, which pre-empts the workflow's own outcome and muddies whether this is a start or complete state.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"The same record without the harness strip, with an unverified/pending digest state appropriate to the start of the workflow and the verify action visible above the tab bar.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"'In-focus product surface' strip with 'Expand' above the heading\",\n        \"Heading 'Checksum evidence record'; subtitle 'Verify digest, file count, byte size, and integrity receipt.'\",\n        \"Step 1: 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified.'\",\n        \"Step 3: 'Receipt links checksum, scope, timestamp, and verifier identity.'\",\n        \"'Package progress' card reduced to its title by the tab bar\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is this recognisable as a start state?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Step 1 already reads 'SHA-256 verified' before any action has been taken\",\n          \"why\": \"Declaring verification complete on the start frame collapses the distinction between start and complete for this workflow.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Does the copy read as real product content?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB'\",\n          \"why\": \"Concrete digest, count, and byte size are exactly what a production checksum record shows; this is the strongest copy in the set.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"e3a0f0b0c4035da789178819dc06284c75c0263f46b79c67617dd7abed93e0ce\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-action\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-action\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Modal titled 'Checksum evidence record' repeating the start frame's five steps verbatim -- including the already-verified 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified' -- then the shared 'Export workspace' block, then a duplicated 'Digest' row at the bottom edge restating step 1. Because step 1 was already 'verified' on the start frame, this action frame carries literally zero state delta from the previous screenshot: same title, same values, same verification claim. Step 2 says 'Source package hash and destination package hash must match' but the two hashes are never displayed side by side, so the comparison the workflow is named for is never shown. No verify control, no in-flight indicator, no controls at all in the viewport, and the community app bar is dropped for a bare 'X'.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verification-in-flight state showing the source and destination hash strings rendered side by side with a live match indicator, and a visible verify/cancel control.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Modal title 'Checksum evidence record' with 'X' close\",\n        \"Step 1 repeats 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified.'\",\n        \"Step 2 promises a source/destination hash comparison that is never rendered\",\n        \"'Export workspace' boilerplate identical to the other action frames\",\n        \"'Digest' row repeated at the bottom, duplicating step 1\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is there any state change relative to the start frame?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"Identical step text including the same 'SHA-256 verified' claim on both frames\",\n          \"why\": \"With no delta in content or status, the action state is indistinguishable from the start state.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the hash comparison shown?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Source package hash and destination package hash must match' with only one checksum value ('9A7F-PORT') on screen\",\n          \"why\": \"Only one side of the comparison exists, so the match cannot be evaluated by the user.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"0c176cfdb7fe9453dd056a3434cd8366b5c35fe38a75cb9ace02a2a472e4334e\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-complete\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-complete\"],\n      \"critique\": \"Correct workflow, community app bar present, heading 'Checksum evidence record' fully visible, and a terminal banner 'Checksum verified -- Checksum evidence shows digest, file count, byte size, verification status, and integrity...' with a verification-seal icon. Combined with step 1's concrete 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified', this is among the more substantiated completions in the set because at least the digest values are real and present. The residual issues: the banner body is clipped by the tab bar mid-word after 'and integrity'; the steps card above is verbatim identical to both the start and action frames so the banner is the sole delta; the destination hash still never appears despite step 2 requiring a match; there is no verification timestamp or verifier identity even though step 3 says the receipt links them; and no follow-on action (view receipt, download) is offered.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A verified-checksum receipt showing both hashes, the match result, the verifier identity and timestamp from step 3, and a fully visible confirmation banner with a next action.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\n        \"Heading 'Checksum evidence record' under the 'Data Portability Community' app bar\",\n        \"Banner 'Checksum verified' with body clipped mid-phrase at 'verification status, and integrity'\",\n        \"Step 1 shows real values: 'Checksum 9A7F-PORT, file count 84, size 18.4 MB, SHA-256 verified.'\",\n        \"No destination hash, verifier identity, or timestamp rendered\",\n        \"Steps card identical to the start and action frames; no post-verification action button\"\n      ],\n      \"directQuestionAnswers\": [\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the completed state legible?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"'Checksum verified' banner with a seal icon, distinct from the 'Package progress' card on the start frame\",\n          \"why\": \"The state change is real and readable, making this one of the few frames where completion is genuinely signalled.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"question\": \"Is the confirmation fully rendered?\",\n          \"visibleEvidence\": \"The banner body ends at 'verification status, and integrity' where the tab bar overlays it\",\n          \"why\": \"The confirmation sentence is cut off, so the user cannot read what the verified evidence includes.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"screenshotHash\": \"ae5419e23cfae5549791fd181169ce95b85d17dadf6de4128d2db58600066ee7\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"redacted-bundle-shows-full-bundle\",\n      \"title\": \"All three export-redacted-bundle screenshots are the export-full-bundle screens\",\n      \"description\": \"B16_ext_export_migration_export-redacted-bundle_start/action/complete.png are byte-identical (sha256 6aacc2fc..., 1e8d1f12..., f1094ba2...) to the corresponding export-full-bundle files. Every one renders the heading or modal title 'Full export bundle', and the complete frame's banner body explicitly reads 'Full export bundle shows contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress, and'. The word 'redacted' never appears as a heading, state label, or outcome on any of the three frames. The redacted-bundle workflow therefore has no visual evidence whatsoever, and a user on these screens would correctly conclude they are in the full-bundle workflow.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Navigate to and capture the actual redacted-bundle surface. Each frame must self-identify as the redacted bundle and show what distinguishes it from the full bundle: which fields were stripped, the redaction count, and the resulting reduced artifact size and checksum.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"import-replay-shows-import-preview\",\n      \"title\": \"export-import-replay action and complete screenshots are the import-preview screens\",\n      \"description\": \"B16_ext_export_migration_export-import-replay_action.png and _complete.png are byte-identical (sha256 3a1f8873..., dc822c23...) to the export-import-preview files of the same states. Both render 'Legacy import preview' as the title/heading, and the complete frame's banner reads 'Import replay ready' -- readiness, not a completed replay. No replay execution, no post-replay row outcomes, and no replay progress appear on either frame. Only the replay start frame contains replay-specific copy, and only inside a subordinate card ('then replay the import with retry and rollback available').\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Capture the distinct replay surface for the action and complete states: replay progress against checkpoint I-118 while running, and afterwards the rows applied vs skipped, the resolved duplicate decisions, and a completion timestamp. The preview workflow's complete banner should also say the preview was completed rather than announcing replay readiness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"action-state-shows-static-explainer\",\n      \"title\": \"Every 'action' screenshot is a static explainer sheet with no controls and no in-progress state\",\n      \"description\": \"All eight action frames (full-bundle, redacted-bundle, transfer-verification, protected-redaction, transfer-rollback, import-preview, import-replay, schema-listing, checksum-evidence) are full-screen modals containing the workflow's numbered 'Export steps' list -- the same list already fully visible on the corresponding start frame -- followed by the identical boilerplate block 'Export workspace / Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' with 'Export scope' and 'Verification and recovery' sub-items. Not one contains a button, spinner, progress bar, percentage, or status chip in the visible viewport, and each ends on a duplicated row that restates step 1 ('Bundle contents', 'Destination', 'Rows preview', 'Schema list', 'Digest', 'Mismatch'). The modals also replace the 'Data Portability Community' app bar with a bare 'X', removing community context. The in-progress state of every workflow in this community is therefore undocumented.\",\n      \"severity\": \"critical-blocker\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-action\"]\n    ,\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Capture the actual in-progress surface for each workflow after the primary action is invoked -- packaging progress, hash comparison in flight, redaction being applied, rollback restoring, scope being toggled -- each with a visible progress or status indicator and at least one control (cancel/abort). Retain the community app bar or an equivalent context label inside the modal, and remove the duplicated step-1 row from the 'Export workspace' block.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"cross-community-copy-leak\",\n      \"title\": \"Copy from other communities (HOA, youth sports) appears in the Data Portability Community\",\n      \"description\": \"The transfer-verification action and complete frames name the destination as 'Provider Cloud HOA' -- a homeowners association -- in a community with no HOA context. The protected-redaction action and complete frames describe the masked data as 'Protected youth profile, minor roster phone, care, vault, payment, and private notes' with policy copy reading 'Each masked field shows guardian or coach visibility policy and the persona allowed to reveal it.' Guardians, coaches, minors, and rosters are youth-sports concepts. The import-replay start frame carries the same leak in a card summary: 'Protected youth roster profile includes minor-da...'. The 'persona allowed to reveal it' phrasing is also inconsistent with this community's legacy flat schema, which has no persona system.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-action\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Replace the borrowed fixture copy with this community's own domain terms: a data-portability destination provider name, protected field examples drawn from this community's schema (member contact, payment, audit fields), and a visibility-policy description that does not reference guardians, coaches, or personas.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"results-described-not-rendered\",\n      \"title\": \"Complete states assert outcome values that the screens never display\",\n      \"description\": \"Every completion banner promises concrete artifact data that no frame renders. 'Export bundle generated' claims to show 'contents, redaction, checksum, file size, download progress' but no filename, size, checksum, or download button appears. 'Transfer verified' claims 'provider, hash match, receipt, timestamp' with no hash pair, provider ID, or timestamp on screen. 'Schema scope saved' claims 'include/exclude scope' with no table list or record count. 'Redaction applied' shows no masked-field count or before/after sample despite step 3 promising 'source label, exported safe value, and redaction count'. 'Import replay ready' claims 'duplicate decisions' with none recorded. Only the checksum workflow renders real values ('9A7F-PORT', 'file count 84', '18.4 MB'), and the rollback complete frame renders real outcome rows -- proving the pattern is achievable elsewhere.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Render the actual result values on each completion screen -- artifact name, byte size, checksum, redaction count, matched hash pair, saved table scope, per-duplicate decisions -- following the pattern the checksum and rollback screens already establish, and offer the appropriate follow-on action (download, view receipt).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"completion-banners-clipped-by-tab-bar\",\n      \"title\": \"Completion banners are truncated mid-sentence by the bottom tab bar on six screens\",\n      \"description\": \"The banner that carries each workflow's outcome is the element being cut off. 'Export bundle generated' ends at 'download progress, and'; 'Transfer verified' is cut immediately after its second line; 'Redaction applied' shows only its title plus a half-height sliver of body text with glyphs sliced through the middle; 'Import replay ready' ends at 'checkpoint, retry and rollback'; 'Schema scope saved' ends at 'include/exclude scope'; 'Checksum verified' ends at 'verification status, and integrity'. On the start frames the same defect hits the 'Package progress' card, which is reduced to a bare title on full-bundle, redacted-bundle, schema-listing, and checksum-evidence, hiding the start action entirely.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-preview-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-complete\", \"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Add bottom padding equal to the tab bar height to the scroll container so terminal banners and the 'Package progress' card render fully, and scroll captures so the state-carrying element is entirely within the viewport.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"truncated-card-titles-and-repeated-shells\",\n      \"title\": \"Card titles truncate mid-word and minimized cards repeat one identical shell\",\n      \"description\": \"Card headings clip to 'Protected field routin...', 'Exportable custom-sc...', and 'Provider transfer roll...' while a 'Minimized' chip beside them consumes roughly a third of the row width. Each such card then renders the same fixed 2x2 grid -- 'Tap for expanded view' / 'Data package' / 'Expand' / 'Generate export' -- so the feed reads as one shell stamped repeatedly. Card summaries compound this: on export-protected-redaction_start both the 'Exportable custom-sc...' card and the 'Full export bundle' card carry the identical string 'Data package includes scope, protected fields, a...', and export-transfer-rollback_start reuses that same string for its 'Provider transfer roll...' card while export-transfer-verification_start gives that same card a completely different body ('Waiting for the export package to be prepared').\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Let card titles wrap to two lines or shrink the 'Minimized' chip so full titles render, and give each card a summary describing its own content rather than a shared boilerplate string.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"empty-lower-region-and-orphaned-chip\",\n      \"title\": \"Transfer screens end in a large empty region, with an unattached 'Waiting' chip on the rollback start\",\n      \"description\": \"export-transfer-verification_start and export-transfer-rollback_start both terminate in a collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure row followed by roughly 400px of uniform empty dark background before the tab bar -- the lower fifth of the screen carries no content where transfer or rollback status belongs. On export-transfer-rollback_start a bare 'Waiting' chip is additionally rendered floating at the right edge in the vertical gap between the 'Package progress' card and the card below it, attached to no container and with no adjacent explanatory label, which reads as a layout escape rather than a designed status indicator.\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Fill the lower region with the transfer/rollback status panel (or expand 'Local package details' by default), and anchor the 'Waiting' chip inside the card whose state it describes with an accompanying label explaining what is being waited on.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"harness-chrome-and-inconsistent-nav\",\n      \"title\": \"'In-focus product surface' harness strip is visible, and the bottom tab bar is inconsistent across screens\",\n      \"description\": \"Four start frames render a dark strip reading 'In-focus product surface' with an 'Expand' affordance directly above the page heading -- capture-harness labelling, not product UI, occupying the position where product context belongs. Separately the bottom tab bar is inconsistent: export-full-bundle, export-redacted-bundle, export-schema-listing, export-checksum-evidence, export-protected-redaction and the import screens show four tabs (Home / Documents / Admin / Messages) with the 'Messages' label clipped at the right edge on several, while export-transfer-verification and export-transfer-rollback show only three tabs (Home / Documents / Messages) with no Admin tab at all. export-protected-redaction_start also clips a row of 'Expand' and 'Generate export' buttons horizontally at the bottom edge, and opens on the severed fragment 'actor are preserved.' cut by the app bar.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-full-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-redacted-bundle-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-schema-listing-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-checksum-evidence-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-verification-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Remove the 'In-focus product surface' harness strip from captured screens, make the tab set consistent across all workflows in this community, and size the tab bar so no label is clipped at the right edge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"findingId\": \"ambiguous-repeated-generate-export\",\n      \"title\": \"Multiple identical 'Generate export' buttons with no scope differentiation\",\n      \"description\": \"export-import-replay_start shows three visually identical 'Generate export' buttons in one viewport: one full-width button below the 'Package progress' card, and one inside each of the two minimized cards ('Protected field routin...' and 'Exportable custom-sc...'). export-protected-redaction_start and export-transfer-rollback_start repeat the pattern. Nothing labels which records each button would export, so the outcome of tapping any of them is unpredictable. Relatedly, export-transfer-rollback_complete leaves a 'Rollback' button enabled alongside a 'Rollback ready' chip on a screen whose body copy already states 'destination status is marked rolled back', with no indication whether pressing it repeats the rollback or is a no-op.\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"status\": \"open\",\n      \"resolved\": false,\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"data-portability-community-export-import-replay-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-protected-redaction-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-start\", \"data-portability-community-export-transfer-rollback-complete\"],\n      \"requiredFix\": \"Scope-label each export action (e.g. 'Generate full bundle', 'Generate this package') or collapse them to a single primary action, and either disable the post-completion 'Rollback' button with a reason or relabel the status chip to a completed state consistent with the body copy.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":15226,"ttft_stream_ms":14484,"time_to_request_ms":12352,"type":"result","duration_ms":633529,"uuid":"fa06f448-7894-4378-8f39-d9893b96ca93"}
